# BMS Data Table Rules

Every list / paginated tabular view in this app must use the shared
`DataTable` component so brand styling (burgundy headers, polished
pagination, etc.) is applied consistently.

## 1. Use the shared component

Import the shared component instead of using Ant Design's `<Table>` directly:

```jsx
import DataTable from '@/common/data/DataTable.jsx';

<DataTable
    columns={columns}
    data={rows}
    loading={loading}
    pagination={paginationConfig}
    showSearch={false}
    showRefresh={false}
    rowKey={(record) => record.id ?? record.uuid}
/>
```

The component lives at `src/common/data/DataTable.jsx`. It already styles:

- **Header row**: solid burgundy `#962E32` background, white text,
  `font-weight: 600`, `2px` darker burgundy underline, single-line cells
  with overflow ellipsis.
- **Hover row**: soft burgundy wash `#fff5f5`.
- **Cell borders**: subtle slate dividers.
- **Pagination** (brand pattern — see section 2 below).

Do not redefine these in scoped `<style>` blocks per usage.

## 2. Pagination

The shared component renders pagination right-aligned with:

- Rounded `10px` page buttons, prev/next, jump prev/next, and page-size
  selector — all with a slate-200 border and slate-700 text.
- Hover: burgundy `#962E32` border + text, `#fff5f5` background.
- Active page: solid burgundy `#962E32` with white text.
- Disabled buttons: light slate background.
- Page size selector matches the same height/radius and uses a burgundy
  focus ring (`box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(150, 46, 50, 0.12)`).
- Top hairline divider above the controls.

When passing `pagination` as a config object, you typically want:

```js
const paginationConfig = {
    current: page,
    pageSize: perPage,
    total,
    showTotal: () => null,        // hide "1-15 of N items"
    showQuickJumper: false,       // hide "Go to" jump input
    onChange: handleChange,
};
```

`showSizeChanger` defaults to `true`; only set `false` when there is
truly no need to choose page size.

## 3. Search and action bar

`DataTable` already renders an optional search input + refresh button row.
Use those props rather than building your own bar above the table:

- `showSearch` (default `true`) — built-in client-side filter input.
- `showRefresh` (default `true`) — refresh button on the right; supply
  `onRefresh` to enable it.
- `rightAction` — provide a custom right-side action (e.g. an "Add"
  button) which replaces the refresh button when provided.

If your page has its own search bar / actions outside the table (e.g.
the Vehicle Management plate-number lookup), set `showSearch={false}`
and `showRefresh={false}` to avoid duplication.

## 4. Don't

- ❌ Do not import `Table` from `antd` directly for tabular data — use
  `DataTable`.
- ❌ Do not duplicate the pagination CSS in scoped `<style>` blocks.
  All brand styling is centralized in `DataTable.jsx`.
- ❌ Do not switch pagination colors away from brand burgundy.
- ❌ Do not render pagination on the left or center; it must stay
  right-aligned with the hairline divider on top.
